 *   2. docs/luma-knowledge-map.md (generated by `php artisan luma:knowledge-map`),
 *   3. the routing self-test (tests/Feature/LumaKnowledgeMapTest.php: every example phrasing must reach its node).
 *
 * Node keys: b = branch number (see the doc), title / title_tl = the follow-up chip, say = example customer phrasings
 * (en, tl, mix = Taglish), kw = trained keywords ("a&b" = both words anywhere in the message), en / tl = the answers,
 * next = child nodes (they become the follow-up chips), buttons = [label_en, label_tl, route], handler = special behaviour.
 *
 * Tone rules for every answer (see docs/luma-tone-rules.md): calm, never defensive, short sentences, plain words,
 * "po" in Tagalog, apologise once and only where something went wrong, never blame the customer, never promise a
 * refund or a date, and never use the words approved or guaranteed. A refund is "requested", "sent" or "reviewed".
 * Numbers come from {{tokens}} (Facts), never typed in.
 */
